{"heroId":76,"art":{"card":"https://assets-bucket.deadlock-api.com/assets-api-res/images/heroes/necro_card.webp","background":"https://assets-bucket.deadlock-api.com/assets-api-res/images/heroes/backgrounds/necro_bg.webp","vertical":"https://assets-bucket.deadlock-api.com/assets-api-res/images/heroes/necro_vertical.webp"},"text":{"en":{"role":"","playstyle":"","lore":"The daughter of high-power defense attorneys, Darcy Graves grew up in a home where every conversation was a debate, argument, or negotiation. It was exhausting. But while her parents were often too busy meeting with clients or working on cases to bond with her, the dead were always there to listen.\n\nGraves enjoyed her time in the cemetery.  It was a quiet place to calm her thoughts and talk through her problems...but one day her one-sided conversations started to change.\n\nIt began with a faint whisper.  A woman's voice that seemed to respond to Graves' complaints.  Intrigued, the teenager listened...and followed the voice's instructions until it guided her to a lead-lined box buried in Van Cortlandt Park.  But while most high school students would freak out if they were to unearth a severed lich hand, Graves was certainly not most teens.  The hand now free of its prison, the lich's voice grew stronger... It had spent years looking to find a student she could pass her knowledge to, and Graves was eager to learn.\n\nNow a fledgling necromancer, Darcy balances not only her homework at Blackmore Academy...but the demands of graveyard denizens, each of whom have their own unfinished business that they seek her aid in resolving.","tags":["Morbid","Area Denial","Necromancer"]},"es":{"role":"","playstyle":"","lore":"Como hija de prestigiosos abogados defensores, Darcy Graves creció en un hogar donde cada conversación era un debate, una discusión o una negociación. Era agotador. Pero mientras sus padres solían estar demasiado ocupados reuniéndose con clientes o trabajando en casos como para pasar tiempo con ella, los muertos siempre estaban ahí para escucharla.\n\nA Graves le gustaba pasar tiempo en el cementerio. Era un lugar tranquilo donde podía calmar sus pensamientos y hablar de sus problemas… pero un día, esas conversaciones unilaterales empezaron a cambiar.\n\nTodo comenzó con un susurro apenas perceptible. La voz de una mujer que parecía responder a los lamentos de Graves. Intrigada, la adolescente escuchó… y siguió las instrucciones de aquella voz hasta que esta la condujo a una caja forrada de plomo, enterrada en Van Cortlandt Park. Pero mientras que la mayoría de estudiantes de instituto entrarían en pánico al desenterrar una mano de lich cercenada, Graves no era como los demás. Liberada de su prisión, la voz del lich se hizo más fuerte… llevaba años buscando a una alumna a la que transmitirle sus conocimientos, y Graves estaba ansiosa por aprender.\n\nAhora, como una joven nigromante, Darcy no solo debe compaginar los deberes de la Academia Blackmore… sino también las exigencias de los habitantes del cementerio, cada uno con sus propios asuntos pendientes, para los que buscan su ayuda.","tags":["Mórbida","Denegadora de áreas","Nigromante"]}},"abilities":{"en":[{"id":3214055642,"slot":1,"ultimate":false,"name":"Jar of Dead","img":"https://assets-bucket.deadlock-api.com/assets-api-res/images/abilities/necro/necro_skull.webp","quip":[],"sections":[{"text":[{"t":"Passive:","dim":true},{"t":" Collect "},{"t":"death","hi":true},{"t":" when anything dies nearby and store it in your Jar of Dead. "},{"t":"Active:","dim":true},{"t":" Throw a jar to summon "},{"t":"Deadheads","hi":true},{"t":" that repeatedly deal "},{"t":"spirit damage","attr":"SpiritDamage","icon":"attr_SpiritDamage"},{"t":" to enemies. Deadheads follow you instead if there's no nearby enemies, and prioritize the target of your weapon."}],"groups":[{"stats":[{"label":"Deadheads","value":"4","unit":"","icon":"https://assets-bucket.deadlock-api.com/assets-api-res/images/upgrades/property_cast.png"},{